course: dictionary
lesson: 954
title: Blossom: flowers and growing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Blossom is a word with two jobs. It can be a noun, meaning the flowers on a tree, or a verb, meaning to produce flowers or to grow well. Context tells you which. «Without that delivery the blossom would never become an apple.» Here blossom is a thing: the flowers that come before fruit.
explain: «It was, to be sure, but a small thing that I asked—merely leave to blossom and expand for yet one more evening...» Here blossom is an action. Ask what would fit: to grow and open out. Swap that meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Blossom can also describe people. When a shy child becomes more confident, we say she has blossomed into a confident speaker. Clue words like «became» or «into» show a change, and the meaning is figurative: growing and developing well.
fact: Blossom means the flowers on a fruit tree or bush, such as apple, cherry or plum, in spring.
fact: A blossom is one of those flowers.
fact: To blossom means to produce flowers, or to grow and develop well.
fact: In science, after bees pollinate the blossom, fruit grows.
fact: In Japan, people celebrate cherry blossom (sakura) with picnics.
exercise: «Without that delivery the blossom would never become an apple.» What is the blossom here? | A ripe apple ready to eat | A type of bee that flies in spring | *The flowers on a tree that come before fruit | A picnic basket
exercise: «...merely leave to blossom and expand for yet one more evening...» What does blossom mean here? | To go to sleep | *To grow and open out | To fall off the tree | To be very quiet
exercise: A shy girl says she will blossom into a confident speaker. What does blossom suggest? | To shout loudly | To produce flowers on her head | To wilt and fade | *To grow and become more confident
test: Which phrase means the flowers of a cherry tree? | cherry red | *cherry blossom | cherry stone | cherry pie
test: A child who was quiet in class starts to blossom. What is the best meaning? | *Grows and becomes happier and more confident | Turns into a flower | Gets lost in the garden | Falls asleep in class
exam: Which sentence uses blossom as a verb? | Bees love the sweet smell of blossom. | A blossom fell onto the path. | *In spring the trees will blossom, and the orchard will be pink. | The apple tree is covered in pink blossom.
